The set that includes star-studded collabs with Bruno Mars and Drake—and is dubbed by fans as “sad Bichota season” due to its melancholic, nostalgia-driven beats and lyrics— debuted No. 1 on the Top Latin Albums chart in August, with 13 of its tracks flooding the Hot Latin Songs chart on its debut week.&nbsp;

It’s most rhythmic tune, “BbY WOW” in collaboration with Judeline and Rusowsky, is currently No. 1 on the Hot Latin Songs, Billboard Global Excl. US, and Billboard Global 200 charts, at the time of publishing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Meanwhile, on tour, the “Bichota” singer invited her friends Becky G, Greeicy, and Elena Rose as her opening acts. “We already have several years of a valuable friendship where obviously we both have very hectic lives, but we always find a moment to hug each other, to ask each other how we are doing,” Elena previously told Billboard .&nbsp;

